    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "I got a bit carried away with the goblin analogy. Let me break it down in a more straightforward way.\n\nAn escrow agent is a neutral third-party service that holds and disburses funds on behalf of the buyer and seller in a real estate transaction. Their primary role is to ensure that the funds are held safely and are released only when the transaction is complete.\n\nIn terms of your specific situation, the escrow agent is responsible for:\n\n* Receiving and holding the earnest money deposit (the \"goblin's ransom\" I mentioned earlier)\n* Paying off any liens or debts associated with the property\n* Releasing the funds to the seller or buyer, depending on the terms of the contract\n* Providing regular statements and updates on the escrow account\n\nThe escrow agent is typically required to act in accordance with the terms of the contract and the laws of the state or local jurisdiction. They are also required to maintain the confidentiality of the transaction and the parties involved.\n\nIn terms of their legal responsibilities to you specifically, the escrow agent is usually required to:\n\n* Provide you with regular statements and updates on the escrow account\n* Ensure that the funds are held safely and are released only when the transaction is complete\n*",
